# Commit after every verified change

After a self-contained, validated slice of work, **commit before starting the next unrelated task**. Do not leave finished work only in a dirty working copy across task boundaries.

This mirrors `AGENTS.md` and `pnpm ui guide vcs`.

## Workflow

1. Validate the slice (focused tests while iterating; broader checks when the slice touches catalog surfaces).
2. Prefer **`jj`** when available (colocated repo):
   - `jj --no-pager st`
   - `jj --no-pager diff --summary`
   - `jj commit -m "Concise why-focused message"` (path-scoped with `-- path…` when unrelated dirty files exist)
   - `jj --no-pager st` to confirm
3. Always pass `-m` / `--message` so commits never open an editor.
4. Do not invent commits for speculative WIP, failing checks, or secrets.
5. Do not push or rewrite published history unless the user asks.

## Cadence

- One logical fix/feature → validate → commit.
- Prefer small commits over an end-of-session dump.
- When the user asks to commit, follow this flow immediately; when finishing verified work without an explicit commit request, still commit per this rule and `pnpm ui guide vcs`.
